course: dictionary
lesson: 14715
title: Big words about buying
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are used mostly by grown-ups at work. Procurement is one of them. Its clues are in the sentence: «The school's procurement officer ordered twenty new books for the library.» Ordering books for a school tells you procurement is about getting things for an organisation.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into a new sentence: «The hospital's buying of new beds went smoothly.» Buying fits, so procurement means getting or buying things, especially for a big group like a school, hospital or government.
explain: Look for other clues too. Words like officer, process and department show it is a job or a set of steps. «The procurement process took three months.» Here it means the whole way of buying, from asking for things to getting them.
explain: Procurement is a noun, and it is usually uncountable, so we say «good procurement», not «a procurements».
fact: Procurement means getting or buying things, especially goods for a company or government.
fact: Procurement can also mean the department or job of buying things for a big organisation.
fact: «Procurement» is a formal word, so you will often meet it in news reports and business talk.
fact: Schools, hospitals and armies all have procurement to buy books, beds or vehicles.
fact: «The procurement process» means the steps for buying, and «procurement officer» means the person who does the buying.
exercise: «The school's procurement officer ordered twenty new books.» What does procurement mean here? | *Getting or buying things for an organisation | Painting the classroom walls | Reading books out loud | Losing things in a cupboard
exercise: «The army's defence procurement team bought new trucks.» What does the team do? | Paints the trucks green | Cleans and fixes the trucks | *Buys things for the army | Drives the trucks to the base
exercise: Which phrase names the person who does the buying for a school? | *A procurement officer | A school cook | A school nurse | A school bell
test: «The hospital's procurement process took six months.» In this sentence, process means | *The steps taken to buy things | A room in the hospital | A type of medicine | A kind of cooking method
test: Which sentence uses procurement correctly? | The procurement ran across the field | *The council's procurement of new buses was approved | She ate two procurements for lunch | The bakery's procurement of flour arrived on Monday
exam: What does procurement mean? | *Getting or buying things, especially for a big organisation | A type of old-fashioned tool | Sending letters to other countries | Keeping things safe in a store
